    clean while/do-while/inf-loop shape the fold rules accept; irreducible /
    head-in-body / nested-interlock loops fall back to `CollapseStructure`
    (honest-partial, never a panic).

    `loopproof` exercises all three loop classes in one function (x86-64, GCC -O0,
    the bytes of a `-c` object loaded at 0x401000).  Source:

        int loopproof(int n, int *a) {
            int i, s = 0;
            i = 0;
            do { s += a[i]; i++; } while (i < n);      // do-while
            for (i = 0; i < n; i++) s += a[i] * 2;     // while / for
            i = 0;
            while (1) { s += a[i]; if (a[i]==0) break; i++; }  // inf-loop + break
            return s;
        }

